1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,043
This is a map you'll draw today:

2
00:00:03,493 --> 00:00:08,711
a dry gully, with a pump house in the middle of it.

3
00:00:09,611 --> 00:00:14,393
And this is the same map as the game reads it.

4
00:00:14,843 --> 00:00:16,583
Twenty-eight lines of text.

5
00:00:18,383 --> 00:00:22,730
You can paint it with the mouse, or type it,

6
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:26,224
and it's the same file either way.

7
00:00:27,424 --> 00:00:30,033
Right-click the ground folder, new file,

8
00:00:30,483 --> 00:00:33,091
and call it gully dot tiles.

9
00:00:33,991 --> 00:00:37,035
It opens in the Tile Map Editor,

10
00:00:37,485 --> 00:00:40,093
and there's nothing to draw yet,

11
00:00:40,543 --> 00:00:42,717
so press the Text button.

12
00:00:44,517 --> 00:00:48,430
The top of an area file is its header.

13
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:51,070
Area is the key,

14
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:55,867
the name the rest of your mission knows it by.

15
00:00:56,767 --> 00:00:59,376
Title is what the crew sees:

16
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:05,478
on the handheld's Beam app, this area will read To The Dry Gully.

17
00:01:06,378 --> 00:01:10,726
Tileset names the file that lists the kinds of ground.

18
00:01:11,626 --> 00:01:14,670
And size is how many cells across,

19
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:18,598
then a small x, and how many down.

20
00:01:19,798 --> 00:01:21,537
Next comes the legend.

21
00:01:22,437 --> 00:01:25,480
Each line is one character, a colon,

22
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:29,409
and a kind of ground from the tileset.

23
00:01:30,309 --> 00:01:32,048
A dot is dust.

24
00:01:32,498 --> 00:01:34,672
A capital W is wall.

25
00:01:36,472 --> 00:01:39,080
Then a line of three dashes,

26
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:42,139
and under them the map itself,

27
00:01:42,589 --> 00:01:44,763
one character for each cell.

28
00:01:45,663 --> 00:01:47,402
There are twelve rows,

29
00:01:47,852 --> 00:01:50,896
and each one is twenty-four characters long.

30
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:54,870
Save it, and run lint.

31
00:01:55,770 --> 00:01:57,509
It comes back clean.

32
00:01:57,959 --> 00:02:02,741
And notice that lint doesn't mention the new file at all.

33
00:02:03,191 --> 00:02:08,409
It only speaks up about a map when something's wrong with it.

34
00:02:09,609 --> 00:02:12,217
Now go back to the picture,

35
00:02:12,667 --> 00:02:16,580
with this button at the top of the text.

36
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:20,120
Two ways to look.

37
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:24,498
Kinds colors each cell by what it is,

38
00:02:24,948 --> 00:02:28,426
and hatches the ones nobody can walk on.

39
00:02:29,326 --> 00:02:32,804
Art draws it the way the game will.

40
00:02:34,604 --> 00:02:36,778
Move the mouse over it,

41
00:02:37,228 --> 00:02:41,576
and the bottom line tells you which cell you're over,

42
00:02:42,026 --> 00:02:43,765
and what it is.

43
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:47,274
And look at the pump house.

44
00:02:47,724 --> 00:02:50,767
It's a box with no way in.

45
00:02:51,967 --> 00:02:54,141
Here's where this is going.

46
00:02:55,041 --> 00:03:00,693
In the game, the pump house has a gap in its west wall,

47
00:03:01,143 --> 00:03:04,187
and the crew walks in through it.

48
00:03:05,987 --> 00:03:09,465
A door on a map is two things.

49
00:03:10,365 --> 00:03:13,409
It's a cell you can walk through,

50
00:03:13,859 --> 00:03:16,033
in a wall you can't.

51
00:03:16,933 --> 00:03:18,672
And it's a mark,

52
00:03:19,122 --> 00:03:23,904
so that later a real door can be stood on it.

53
00:03:25,704 --> 00:03:29,183
Plus Entry gives me a new legend line.

54
00:03:29,633 --> 00:03:31,372
The kind is floor,

55
00:03:31,822 --> 00:03:33,996
the mark is pump door,

56
00:03:34,446 --> 00:03:37,489
and the character is a capital D.

57
00:03:38,389 --> 00:03:41,433
Then I paint one cell with it,

58
00:03:41,883 --> 00:03:44,926
in the middle of the west wall.

59
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:50,639
Press Text, and look at what the editor wrote.

60
00:03:51,539 --> 00:03:54,148
One new line in the legend,

61
00:03:54,598 --> 00:03:57,641
and one changed character in the map.

62
00:03:58,091 --> 00:03:59,830
Nothing else was touched.

63
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:04,509
When the transporter puts somebody in the gully,

64
00:04:04,959 --> 00:04:10,176
this is where they'll stand, at the west end of the map.

65
00:04:11,976 --> 00:04:16,324
The party needs somewhere to stand when it beams down.

66
00:04:17,224 --> 00:04:21,137
So I make a second mark the same way,

67
00:04:21,587 --> 00:04:24,630
on open ground at the west end.

68
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:29,474
The mark gives that cell a name,

69
00:04:29,924 --> 00:04:31,663
and it's still dust.

70
00:04:32,563 --> 00:04:35,607
Then one more line in the header.

71
00:04:36,057 --> 00:04:39,100
Entry, and the name of the mark.

72
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:44,813
The editor has a tool for this as well,

73
00:04:45,263 --> 00:04:47,872
and it writes the cell's numbers.

74
00:04:48,772 --> 00:04:50,511
Both of them work.

75
00:04:50,961 --> 00:04:52,700
The name is better,

76
00:04:53,150 --> 00:04:58,802
because it still points at the right place after you redraw the map.

77
00:05:00,002 --> 00:05:03,480
Lint reads your maps along with everything else.

78
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:06,120
Misspell the entry line,

79
00:05:06,570 --> 00:05:12,222
and it tells you the name is neither a mark nor a cell.

80
00:05:13,122 --> 00:05:16,600
Type a letter that isn't in the legend,

81
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:20,963
and it tells you the whole area won't load.

82
00:05:22,763 --> 00:05:24,502
It warns you, too,

83
00:05:24,952 --> 00:05:27,996
when two files claim the same area,

84
00:05:28,896 --> 00:05:33,678
and when a row is longer than the size line says.

85
00:05:35,478 --> 00:05:38,522
But there are things it can't see.

86
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:43,335
Leave a space in the middle of a row,

87
00:05:43,785 --> 00:05:48,133
and that cell is a hole nobody can walk on.

88
00:05:49,033 --> 00:05:54,250
So compare your file with the page, one character at a time.

89
00:05:55,450 --> 00:05:59,363
Nothing in the mission leads to the gully yet.

90
00:06:00,263 --> 00:06:03,741
But the ship's transporter can put you there.

91
00:06:05,541 --> 00:06:07,280
Beam down as usual,

92
00:06:07,730 --> 00:06:10,339
then open Beam on the handheld.

93
00:06:10,789 --> 00:06:15,137
There's one other place on the list, and it's yours.

94
00:06:16,037 --> 00:06:18,646
You're standing on your own mark.

95
00:06:19,546 --> 00:06:21,720
Click inside the pump house,

96
00:06:22,170 --> 00:06:26,083
and you walk in through the gap you painted.

97
00:06:27,883 --> 00:06:30,926
For the exercise, try the other tools.

98
00:06:31,376 --> 00:06:34,420
Draw a second building with the rectangle,

99
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:39,652
then break the file on purpose and read what lint says.

100
00:06:41,452 --> 00:06:45,365
Next time, you join this map to the yard.
